n these vehicles by 2025. Annotate the diagram to show the change in consumer surplus in the market for diesel vehicles, following the change in demand caused by the proposed 2025 ban in some city centres.","topics":["1-2-8-producer-consumer-surplus","1-2-2-demand"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["consumer surplus","fall in demand","diesel vehicles","diagram"],"qpPage":4,"msPage":5,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-as-p1-2018-jun-q5a","p":29,"section":"A","questionNumber":"5(a)","parentQuestion":"5","choiceGroup":null,"marks":1,"questionText":"The British Broadcasting Corporation (BBC) is a TV broadcaster. It is financed through an annual TV licence fee of £145.50. At this fee level many TV owners benefit from consumer surplus. Define the term ‘consumer surplus’.","topics":["1-2-8-producer-consumer-surplus"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["consumer surplus","definition"],"qpPage":9,"msPage":8,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-as-p1-2016-jun-q6c","p":27,"section":"B","questionNumber":"6(c)","parentQuestion":"6","choiceGroup":null,"marks":6,"questionText":"Explain the likely impact on producer surplus of an increase in the demand for housing. Use a diagram to illustrate your answer.","topics":["1-2-8-producer-consumer-surplus"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["producer surplus","housing","demand","surplus diagram"],"qpPage":10,"msPage":12,"ctxPage":9,"modelAnswer":null}]}
